,"url":"/docs/components/tooltip#features","content":"Flips and shifts to stay in the viewport"},"1659":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-18","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#features","content":"Configurable open and close delays"},"1660":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-19","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#default","content":"Use it with `TooltipTrigger`, which wraps both the tooltip content and a focusable element such as a `Button`. The tooltip appears on hover and focus."},"1661":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-20","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#custom-anchor","content":"To position a tooltip relative to a different focusable element, use the `triggerRef` prop. `TooltipTrigger` still handles showing and hiding on hover and focus."},"1662":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-21","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#customization","content":"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."},"1663":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-22","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#keyboard","content":"Key"},"1664":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-23","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#keyboard","content":"Action"},"1665":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-24","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#keyboard","content":"`Tab`"},"1666":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-25","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#keyboard","content":"Moves focus to the focusable element and shows the tooltip"},"1667":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-26","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#keyboard","content":"`Escape`"},"1668":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-27","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#keyboard","content":"Closes the tooltip"},"1669":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-28","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#aria","content":"The tooltip uses `role=\"tooltip\"` and is associated with its focusable element via `aria-describedby`"},"1670":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-29","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#best-practices","content":"Keep tooltip content short and informative."},"1671":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-30","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#best-practices","content":"Tooltips are not shown on touch screen interactions. Ensure your UI is usable without tooltips."},"1672":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-31","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#best-practices","content":"Do not place interactive content inside tooltips. Use a `Popover` instead."},"1673":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"page","content":"DonutChart","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components","Chart"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart"},"1674":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","content":"Donut charts are for parts-to-whole comparison—how partial elements add up to a total—shown as a ring so a few categories are easy to compare at a glance."},"1675":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#installation","content":"Installation"},"1676":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#examples","content":"Examples"},"1677":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#default","content":"Default"},"1678":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#single-slice","content":"Single slice"},"1679":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#legend-placement","content":"Legend placement"},"1680":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#small-slices","content":"Small slices"},"1681":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#format-value","content":"Format value"},"1682":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#props","content":"Props"},"1683":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#donutchart","content":"DonutChart"},"1684":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#default","content":"You give the chart a `data` array (`id`, `name`, `value`) and a `label` in the middle - this is the everyday setup when you want several categories on one ring and a headline number or title in the hole."},"1685":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#single-slice","content":"When there is only one slice, the ring is full. Add `subLabel` if you want a smaller second line under the main center text."},"1686":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#legend-placement","content":"Switch `legend` to `right` to sit the legend beside the donut, or `bottom` to stack it underneath. `legendLabel` is there when you want a title above the legend items."},"1687":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#small-slices","content":"Very thin slices can be noisy to hover. Anything at or below `smallSliceThreshold` (default `0.05` of the total) is treated as “small,” and if those slices sit next to each other on the ring, one hover opens a single tooltip that lists the whole group."},"1688":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-14","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#format-value","content":"Use `formatValue` when the raw numbers in the tooltip should read like money, counts with separators, or whatever your product expects. The percentage of the total still formats on its own; your function only shapes the value column."},"1689":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","type":"page","content":"Bar Chart","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components","Chart"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart"},"1690":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","content":"A flexible, accessible, and design-aligned data visualization solution for di